# ============================================================
# Construction OS — Mobile (apps/mobile, Expo) env template
# ============================================================
# Two-file scheme (only these two exist — spec §08):
#   apps/mobile/.env.example  ← THIS committed template (dev / staging / prod)  [committed]
#   apps/mobile/.env          ← concrete active file, filled per environment     [gitignored]
# Set up:  cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env   then fill values (dev defaults already work).
# KEEP IN SYNC: apps/mobile/.env and apps/mobile/.env.example must carry the SAME KEYS.
#
# Expo INLINES every EXPO_PUBLIC_* var into the JS bundle at Metro start — these are PUBLIC by
# design and must NEVER hold a secret. The mobile app is a Keycloak public OIDC client (PKCE,
# ADR-050); it has no client secret. Point the issuer at the realm that actually exists for the
# environment — the local Keycloak imports `construction-os-dev`, so the dev default targets it
# (the code default falls back to `construction-os`, which 404s locally).
# ============================================================

# staging:     EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://auth.staging.construction-os.io/realms/construction-os
# production:  EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://auth.construction-os.io/realms/construction-os
EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://localhost:8090/realms/construction-os-dev
EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=cos-mobile
